% ============================================================================
% heat-causes-phase-change.query.adj — worked recall over the heat/phase-change
% causal library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does heating (or
% cooling) a substance cause?" — it states no physics fact of its own — it
% only `import`s the grounded table+rule and asks binding queries. The answer
% is DERIVED, composing the new heat-direction fact with the already-shipped
% `phase_change_name` table, so every answer carries BOTH citations in its
% `steps` trail.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli heat-causes-phase-change.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "heat-causes-phase-change.adj"

? causes_phase_change(heating, $Name)   % expect melting, vaporization
? causes_phase_change(cooling, $Name)   % expect freezing, condensation
